      "text": "WAL growth after importer run\nDuring Tuesday’s import, the WAL grew faster than the daily dashboard refresh could recycle it. I checked the process list and found importer PID 614 still writing the final batch, so I left the database alone instead of forcing a checkpoint. Once the process exits, run `PRAGMA wal_checkpoint(TRUNCATE)` during the quiet window and note the before-and-after file size in the runbook. The scheduled report query still completes normally, so there is no reason to restart the application. If the file remains large the next morning, compare the import duration with the prior week before changing retention settings.",
