      "id": "f003",
      "text": "A steadier bedtime helped this week\nFor five nights I left my phone charging in the hall instead of beside the bed. I read a few pages of a mystery novel and turned the lamp off before I felt drowsy, rather than checking the clock. I averaged about seven and a half hours of sleep and felt clearer during the morning commute. The change was small enough to repeat even on the late grocery night. I am keeping the notebook by the kettle so I can jot down whether the routine still feels easy next week; I do not want to turn it into another strict scorecard.",
